  "formalFindings": [
    "African Studies is the English full-time BA; Article 2.2 defines no formal specialisations. Programme themes remain valid academic interests.",
    "The new Appendix F column applies from 2026–2027. Its second year names 55 EC and an additional required T.B.A. 5 EC at level 200. Outgoing year-2 Swahili II is a 10-EC resit; new Swahili III is 5 EC.",
    "Both third-year Anthropological Linguistics and African Religions are required 5-EC components. The old choice group does not apply. The 0-EC thesis seminar adds no credit.",
    "Article 4.2 requires Swahili I before II, I and II before III, propaedeutic completion before Study in Africa, and propaedeutic completion and Study in Africa before the thesis."
  ],
  "officialAlternative": "Inspected the current official regulatory index, its linked programme-specific 2026–2027 OER, current programme-structure page, current programme catalogue API, both Swahili II entries and African Languages Lab. Targeted official-source searches also located African Networks and African Religions, already counted in years 1 and 3. None of the inspected material identifies the T.B.A. component or an explicit cohort bridge; no absence of an amendment outside the inspected material is claimed.",
